  "causal_interpretation": "A campaign cannot be economically new merely because the same close observes that yesterday's exit order filled. That close is the first reconciliation of flat inventory after the failed campaign. Using it simultaneously to declare reference recovery conflates settlement of the old campaign with admission of a new one. The next structural test should require the symbol to have already been observed flat at a prior close before score-reference rearm can create a new campaign. This is an inventory lifecycle condition, not a fixed N-day cooldown.",
